  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the baby as the survivor",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the newborn baby, who is depicted as the survivor ('i made it out alive'). The text 'i made it out alive' and 'the democrats didn't get me' uses the first-person pronoun 'me' to directly address the viewer, implying that the user identifies with the baby as the survivor. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user sees themselves as the vulnerable subject who narrowly escaped harm due to the non-action or inaction of 'the democrats'. The baby's visual material is central to this projection, as it embodies the vulnerability and relief of survival.",
